---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import { routeFor } from "../../i18n";
---

<DocLayout
  lang="en"
  page="docs/roadmap"
  title="Roadmap"
  intro="A public-alpha view of what already works, what is rough, and where Opaline is heading next."
  next={[
    { href: routeFor("en", "docs/html-format"), label: "HTML format" },
    { href: routeFor("en", "docs/storage"), label: "Storage architecture" },
  ]}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Current alpha</h2>
    <ul class="status-list">
      <li><span class="status-icon done">✓</span><span><strong>implemented</strong> Local workspace creation, HTML note editing, recent documents, Today’s log, settings, and language switching.</span></li>
      <li><span class="status-icon done">✓</span><span><strong>implemented</strong> Unified editor command registry, slash command menu, and command palette.</span></li>
      <li><span class="status-icon done">✓</span><span><strong>implemented</strong> Relationship surfaces including Links from this note, Mentions this note, and a Relationship map.</span></li>
      <li><span class="status-icon partial">◐</span><span><strong>partial</strong> Extension widgets, update checking, AI provider settings, import/export flows, and the AI editing protocol have entry points or infrastructure but need more validation.</span></li>
      <li><span class="status-icon planned">○</span><span><strong>planned</strong> Stronger workspace migration, richer publishing, semantic retrieval, and a complete AI note-generation experience.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is still rough</h2>
    <p>The alpha is useful for trying the workbench model, but it should not be treated as a finished data system. Back up important workspaces before serious use.</p>
    <div class="doc-grid">
      <article class="doc-card">
        <h3>Packaging</h3>
        <p>Windows and macOS Apple Silicon assets are available for v0.1.2. Intel macOS and Linux still need explicit build and test coverage.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="doc-card">
        <h3>Updater</h3>
        <p>The manual update UI now uses signed GitHub Release metadata for Windows x64 and macOS Apple Silicon, and still needs broader install testing.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="doc-card">
        <h3>Data safety</h3>
        <p>HTML remains the durable source, while SQLite indexes and metadata should continue to be rebuildable.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="doc-card">
        <h3>AI workflow</h3>
        <p>The editor command protocol is wired in, but AI note generation still needs source display, change previews, and user confirmation flows.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Next direction</h2>
    <p>Near-term work should make the alpha safer to run every day: continue polishing the editor experience, improve workspace migration, stabilize extension APIs, and document update distribution before enabling automatic updates.</p>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
